EXECUTABLE producer

DESCRIPTION
  Reads input.txt and sends its contents as the body of one HTTP POST to
  localhost:9812. The header and body are sent as two separate sends, so the
  consumer reliably reads the header on its first recv and the body on its
  second. After sending, the producer blocks on a receive so the connection
  stays open (no abortive close discarding unread data) until the consumer has
  read everything and closed its end; only then does the producer close.

ENTRY
  pathin = "input.txt"
  file = CALL read-file-all pathin
  hdr = CALL t2-build-header
  sock = CALL socket 2 1
  sa = CALL make-sockaddr 9812 16777343
  CALL connect sock.fd sa.addr sa.addr_len -> cstatus
  DISCARD cstatus
  CALL send sock.fd hdr.header hdr.length -> sent1
  DISCARD sent1
  CALL send sock.fd file.data file.length -> sent2
  DISCARD sent2
  ack = CALL receive sock.fd 16
  DISCARD ack.buffer
  DISCARD ack.bytes_received
  CALL close-socket sock.fd -> cs
  DISCARD cs
END_EXECUTABLE
